---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageIntro from '../PageIntro.astro';
import { organization, specification, sdks, url } from '../../../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="ANS implementations"
  description="Explore the ANS reference implementation, Go, Rust, and Java SDKs, gateway integrations, OpenShell research preview, and related Trust Index work."
>
  <PageIntro
    title="Software you can build with."
    description="Explore the code you can build with today, the examples you can learn from, and the previews you can help shape."
  />
  <section class="container content-section">
    <h2>Core implementation and SDKs</h2>
    <div class="rows">
      <article class="integration-row">
        <div>
          <h3>Registration Authority and Transparency Log</h3>
          <p class="kind">Reference implementation</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>
            A Go implementation of the registration lifecycle and transparency
            services, with local demos and an offline verifier. Run it to
            understand the protocol or evaluate your own deployment.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href={`${organization}/ans`}>
            Explore ans
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>
      {sdks.map((sdk) => (
        <article class="integration-row">
          <div>
            <h3>{sdk.name}</h3>
            <p class="kind">{sdk.label}</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p>
              {sdk.detail} Check the repository’s releases and documentation for
              the exact supported API and verification features.
            </p>
            <a class="text-link" href={`${organization}/${sdk.repo}`}>
              Explore {sdk.repo}
            </a>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container content-section">
    <h2>Integrations and examples</h2>
    <div class="rows">
      <article class="integration-row">
        <div>
          <h3>agentgateway and Agent Router</h3>
          <p class="kind">Verifier and gateway recipes</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>
            <code>ans-gateway-auth</code> verifies ANS-6 Method B callers
            through Envoy’s external authorization protocol. It includes gateway
            recipes and end-to-end suites for agentgateway and Agent Router.
          </p>
          <p>
            Support for other Envoy-compatible gateways depends on their
            configuration and request forwarding. The repository documents that
            coverage boundary.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href={`${organization}/ans-gateway-auth`}>
            Source and deployment recipes
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="integration-row">
        <div>
          <h3>NVIDIA OpenShell</h3>
          <span class="chip chip--preview">Research preview</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>
            <code>ans-openshell</code> adds signing middleware and destination
            registration checks outside an agent’s sandbox, keeping its identity
            key out of the sandbox.
          </p>
          <p>
            Its upstream extension contracts are previews. Destination
            registration checks do not implement ANS-6 binding to the actual TLS
            peer certificate; see the repository’s security notes.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href={`${organization}/ans-openshell`}>
            Explore the research preview
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="integration-row">
        <div>
          <h3>A2A, MCP and HTTP</h3>
          <p class="kind">SDK examples</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>
            Use the SDK examples as starting points for adding ANS verification
            to protocol clients and services. Protocol compatibility still
            requires an application to wire in and enforce verification.
          </p>
          <ul class="links">
            <li>
              <a
                class="text-link"
                href={`${organization}/ans-sdk-java/tree/main/ans-sdk-agent-client/examples`}
              >
                Java protocol examples
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a
                class="text-link"
                href={`${organization}/ans-sdk-rust/blob/main/crates/ans-verify/examples/mcp_mtls_client.rs`}
              >
                Rust MCP client
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="band band--deep">
    <div class="container content-section">
      <h2>Related work</h2>
      <div class="panels panels--2">
        <article>
          <h3>Discovery profile: DNS-AID alignment</h3>
          <p>
            The published <code>ANS_DNSAID</code> profile uses SVCB records for
            endpoint discovery. ANS adds registration and authentication
            evidence. Read the profile for its current record format.
          </p>
          <ul class="links">
            <li>
              <a
                class="text-link"
                href={`${specification}/blob/main/spec/discovery-profiles/ans-dnsaid.md`}
              >
                Read the profile
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Separate project: trust evaluation</h3>
          <p>
            The Trust Index specification and Agent Trust Discovery reference
            implementation explore scoring with ANS evidence and other signals.
            Scoring is separate from ANS authentication; the implementation
            documents deferred features.
          </p>
          <ul class="links">
            <li>
              <a class="text-link" href={`${organization}/trust-index-spec`}>
                Trust Index specification
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a
                class="text-link"
                href={`${organization}/agent-trust-discovery`}
              >
                Reference implementation
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container content-section">
    <div class="split split--prose">
      <h2>Bring your framework.</h2>
      <div class="stack">
        <p>
          A framework can call an ANS SDK, API, or gateway verifier, but an
          integration must enforce the verification result in the request path.
          Adding a tool to an agent’s tool list alone does not guarantee that it
          will be used.
        </p>
        <p>
          Have an adapter to share? Open an issue with the public source,
          installation instructions, supported ANS features, and tests that
          demonstrate rejected invalid requests.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href={url('community/')}>
          Contribute an integration
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
